_score_accruals":63.8,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.18443524150170162,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":61.6,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.013992792214735955,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":82.5,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":0.0055261821252600846,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":2.8,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.114544041576401,"_gp_roic_consistency":true,"_score_roic_consistency":80.9,"_gate_incr_roic":0.057764190706058864,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":35.9,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.061436952309247894,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":12.9,"_gate_pool_share":-0.06477382018476929,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":14.1,"_gate_rev_durability":0.04343337013513948,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":46.7,"_gate_fcf_durability":-0.016089692854926896,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":17.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.02994717427931071,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":44.4,"_gate_share_shrink":0.01432531364400269,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":32.1,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.00416,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":2.8,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"DTE Energy Company engages in energy-related businesses and services. The company operates through four segments: Electric, Gas, DTE Vantage, and Energy Trading. The company's Electric segment generates, purchases, distributes, and sells electricity to approximately 2.3 million residential, commercial, and industrial customers in southeastern Michigan. It generates electricity through coal-fired plants, natural gas plant, hydroelectric pumped storage, and nuclear plants, as well as wind and solar assets. This segment owns and operates 702 distribution substations with a capacity of approximately 37,870,000 kilovolt-amperes (kVA) and approximately 4,56,900 line transformers with a capacity of approximately 33,770,000 kVA. The company's Gas segment purchases, stores, transports, distributes, and sells natural gas to approximately 1.4 million residential, commercial, and industrial customers throughout Michigan; and sells storage and transportation capacity. This segment has approximately 21,000 miles of distribution mains; 1,242,000 service pipelines; and 1,361,000 active meters, as well as owns approximately 2,000 miles of transmission pipelines. Its DTE Vantage segment offers metallurgical and petroleum coke to steel and other industries; and power generation, steam production, chilled water production, and wastewater treatment services, as well as compressed air supply to industrial customers. This segment also owns and operates 2 renewable generating plants with a capacity of 70 MWs; and 22 gas recovery sites. Its Energy Trading segment engages in power, natural gas, and environmental marketing and trading; structured transactions; and the optimization of contracted natural gas pipeline transportation and storage positions. The company was founded in 1849 and is based in Detroit, Michigan.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Joi M. Harris | President, CEO & Director | Age 55 | Compensation: $2.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 9K people. Revenue per employee of $1.7M ranks in the top quartile among Utilities peers. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["DTE Energy Company is a large-cap utilities business with a $29.1B market cap on $15.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -6% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Utilities peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Price sits 26% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.26172875705757853},{"text":"Regulatory rate-case risk and rising cost of capital \u2014 the allowed return is set by commissions, and the business lives or dies by that negotiation.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Grid modernisation capex burden \u2014 aging infrastructure requires massive reinvestment that regulators may not fully allow into rate base, compressing earned returns.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Wildfire and climate liability \u2014 extreme weather events create catastrophic, uninsurable losses that can push even investment-grade utilities toward restructuring.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","64 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Benson transition team draws criticism over DTE, MEDC ties","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/benson-transition-team-draws-criticism-163000000.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794587594.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.7,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Nessel scrutinizes DTE plans for Google data center in Van Buren Twp.","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/nessel-scrutinizes-dte-plans-google-050228000.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794546197.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"DTE Crews Have Trimmed 56 of 80 Planned Miles in the Grosse Pointes and Detroit\u2019s East Side, and Yard Trees Marked With a White X Are Coming Down","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/dte-crews-trimmed-56-80-200000000.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794427409.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.273,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"DTE schedules planned power outages in Dearborn Heights for Wednesday","source":"clickondetroit.com","link":"https://www.clickondetroit.com/news/local/2026/11/11/dte-schedules-planned-power-outages-in-dearborn-heights-for-wednesday/","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794406353.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is DTE (NYSE:DTE) Feeling Data Center Load Build?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/utility/is-dte-nysedte-feeling-data-center-load-build","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794403320.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"DTE honors nearly 1,000 employees for their service on Veterans Day","source":"cbsnews.com","link":"https://www.cbsnews.com/detroit/news/dte-honors-nearly-1000-employees-veterans-day/","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp"